      "summary": {
        "kind": "Summary",
        "text": "This retrospective INSPIRE study compared preoperative models with models incorporating low-frequency intraoperative data for stage 2 or 3 postoperative acute kidney injury. Intraoperative summaries added limited discrimination, and a temporal deep-learning model did not outperform simpler tabular methods. The findings motivate testing whether higher-resolution physiologic signals add information beyond the preoperative record.",
