      "summary": {
        "kind": "Summary",
        "text": "This preprint evaluates conversational segmentation across seven medical-imaging modalities and audits dermoscopy performance by skin-tone group. Performance varied substantially by modality, with weaker results on some radiologic targets. Differences in mask generation and overlap across the audited skin-tone groups show why aggregate benchmark performance can conceal important failure modes.",
